    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "SPACIOUS B-RATED FOUR-BEDROOM BUNGALOW ON A GENEROUS C.1-ACRE MATURE SITE, BEAUTIFUL GARDENS, MODERN UPGRADES AND EXCELLENT FAMILY ACCOMMODATION, CONVENIENTLY LOCATED JUST OFF THE N3\n\nSmith Property proudly present this impressive detached four-bedroom bungalow to the market, occupying a generous site of approximately 0.41 hectares (c.1 acre) at Tullytreane, Crosskeys, Co. Cavan.\n\nBuilt circa 2006, this substantial family home offers bright, spacious and exceptionally versatile accommodation, both inside and out. Having been carefully maintained and upgraded by the current owners, the property combines generous living space, modern comforts and an excellent energy rating with extensive mature gardens and a superb range of outdoor features.\n\nThe property is particularly well suited to family life, offering four generously proportioned double bedrooms, spacious living accommodation, a large open-plan kitchen/dining area, sunroom, utility/laundry facilities and excellent additional attic space.\n\nThe accommodation is complemented by a number of recent improvements, including recently upgraded triple-glazed windows and external doors, a completely redesigned and modernised main bathroom, solar panels contributing to the property`s hot water requirements and a number of other improvements throughout the home.\n\nThe property has a B-rated BER, providing an important sustainable advantage for prospective purchasers. The combination of the property`s energy rating, upgraded triple glazing, insulation, solar technology and oil-fired central heating provides a comfortable and efficient home, while its B rating may also make the property attractive to purchasers who are eligible for green mortgage products, subject to the individual lender`s criteria and lending terms.\n\nAt the heart of the home is a particularly impressive bright and spacious living room, featuring recessed lighting and a freestanding stove which creates an attractive focal point while providing an additional source of heat. Double doors connect the living space with the kitchen/dining area, creating an excellent sense of flow throughout the principal living accommodation.\n\nThe open-plan kitchen and dining area provides an excellent space for everyday family life and entertaining, with a generous fitted kitchen, integrated appliances and ample room for a large dining table. Recessed lighting further enhances the bright and spacious feel of this area.\n\nThe kitchen opens through to a large and bright sunroom with tiled roof, providing an additional reception/living space and enjoying views towards the rear gardens. Double doors lead directly from the sunroom onto the patio area, creating an excellent connection between the internal and external living spaces.\n\nA spacious utility room and laundry area is located to the rear of the property, providing excellent practical storage and workspace, with convenient access towards the rear garden.\n\nThe four bedrooms are all generously proportioned. The bedroom accommodation provides excellent flexibility for a growing family, guests or those requiring dedicated working or hobby space. Two of the bedrooms are served by a Jack-and-Jill style ensuite arrangement, adding further practicality to the accommodation.\n\nThe main bathroom has been completely redesigned and refurbished, creating a modern and attractive space with strong contemporary appeal.\n\nThe property benefits from a large open-plan heated attic space with storage and excellent natural light from Velux windows.\n\n \n\nThe space offers excellent flexibility and would suit a home office, playroom, games room, hobby area, studio or additional storage. There may also be potential to convert the attic to additional habitable accommodation, subject to the necessary planning, building regulations, fire safety and statutory requirements.\n\nThe property occupies a generous c.1-acre site with gated entrance, substantial boundary piers and mature gardens.\n\nThe grounds include lawned areas, established planting, a walled patio with pergola, trellis and fruit bushes, together with a large storage shed featuring an insulated roof, windows and door.\n\nA substantial polytunnel is also included, making the property particularly suitable for those with an interest in gardening and growing.\n\nTullytreane enjoys a peaceful rural setting just off the N3, while remaining convenient to local amenities.\n\nCrosskeys is approximately 2.5 3km away, with a primary school, creche, shop, church, community and sporting facilities.\n\nBallyjamesduff is approximately 5km drive, offering a wider range of shops, schools, childcare, medical and recreational facilities, while Cavan Town is approximately 15km drive.\n\nThe location provides excellent access to the N3 and surrounding towns, making this an ideal family home combining spacious accommodation, a generous site, mature gardens and convenient accessibility.\n\n\n"
      },
